-- title:
--   Only r-power reduced norms act by r-power isogenies
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, rationals $a,b$ and a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ containing every rational integer, a level $N$, an algebraically closed field $k_0$ and a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of type $(\Lambda,N)$ over $k_0$ (an abelian scheme of relative dimension $2$ with commutative relative group law, a $\Lambda$-action and level data). Fix further rationals $a_1,b_1$, a submodule $R_1\subseteq H:=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ that is an order (contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $H$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated), a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$, and a subgroup $\Gamma_t\le H^{\times}$ whose elements are exactly those of `awayUnits R₁ v`, i.e. the units lying, at every $w\ne v$, in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. Given a map $e$ from $\Gamma_t$ to endomorphisms of $A_0.A$ over the base; the hypothesis (E4) that for every algebraically closed $k_0$-algebra field $k$, every fake elliptic curve $A$ over $k$ and every $g_A:A.A\to A_0.A$ exhibiting $A$ as the pullback of $A_0$ along $k_0\to k$ (cartesian, compatible with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level), any level-preserving $\varphi$ over the base forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^d$ with some $\psi$ satisfies $\varphi\circ A.\mathrm{act}(r^i)$ followed by $g_A$ equal to $g_A$ followed by $e\gamma\circ A_0.\mathrm{act}(r^j)$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ and $i,j\in\mathbb{N}$; and a submodule $R_2\le R_1$ which is $r$-saturating in $R_1$ (each $x\in R_1$ has $r^c x\in R_2$) together with a map $\hat e$ from $R_2$ to endomorphisms of $A_0.A$ over the base which is level-preserving, satisfies $\hat e(xy)=\hat e(y)$ followed by $\hat e(x)$, sends an integer $m$ to $A_0.\mathrm{act}(m)$, agrees with $e\gamma$ up to $r$-power multiplications whenever $x=r^k\gamma$ (E5d), and is injective. Then for every $z\in R_2$, every endomorphism $\psi$ of $A_0.A$ and every $j$, if $(\hat e(z),\psi)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^j$ for $A_0$, there are $i,t\in\mathbb{N}$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(z)\,r^i=r^t$ or $\mathrm{nrd}(z)\,r^i=-r^t$, where $\mathrm{nrd}$ is the reduced norm $z_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a_1z_{\mathrm{I}}^2-b_1z_{\mathrm{J}}^2+a_1b_1z_{\mathrm{K}}^2$.
--
--   This is the norm constraint in the Čerednik–Drinfeld analysis of endomorphisms of fake elliptic curves over an algebraically closed field of residue characteristic $r$: an element of the order acting through an isogeny of $r$-power degree must have reduced norm an $r$-power up to sign and up to $r$-power factors. It is used in the construction of the Atkin–Lehner and Hecke dictionaries attached to an endomorphism dictionary with full endomorphism algebra.
